<article class="env-corollary" id="0619">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0619">Corollary <span data-tag="0619">9.1.5.13</span>.</a> Let $F: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be a functor of $\infty $-categories and let $\kappa $ be an infinite cardinal. If $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is $\kappa $-filtered and $F$ is right cofinal, then $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ is also $\kappa $-filtered. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\lambda $ be a regular cardinal of exponential cofinality $\geq \kappa $ such that $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ and $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ are essentially $\lambda $-small. It follows from Proposition <a data-tag="05Y1" href="/tag/05Y1">9.1.5.10</a> (together with Proposition <a data-tag="05XH" href="/tag/05XH">7.7.7.1</a>) that $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ is $\kappa $-filtered if and only if, for every $\kappa $-small simplicial set $K$, the limit functor $\varprojlim : \operatorname{Fun}(K, \operatorname{\mathcal{S}}_{&lt; \lambda } ) \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{S}}_{&lt; \lambda }$ preserves $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$-indexed colimits. Since $F$ is right cofinal, it will suffice to show that $\varprojlim $ preserves $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$-indexed colimits (Corollary <a data-tag="02NV" href="/tag/02NV">7.2.2.8</a>), which follows from our assumption that $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is $\kappa $-filtered. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</article>
